/target/

# Runtime state: the event log, the workspace index, the lease. Machine-local,
# rebuilt on demand, and never evidence of anything.
/.poorai/*

# Results are not runtime state.
#
# Evaluation reports, calibration profiles and capability evidence are what a
# promotion decision cites, and they lived only on the machine that produced
# them -- so a number in the roadmap could not be checked against the artifact
# behind it by anyone without that machine. They are content-addressed and
# never overwritten, so tracking them adds rather than churns.
!/.poorai/calibrations/
!/.poorai/models/

# Evaluation reports stay untracked until the corpus is re-run.
#
# Every campaign recorded before 2026-09-03 is void: the tool-failure rate was
# never measured, the context reaching the backend was not the one calibrated,
# and a workspace with no checks scored as resolved. Committing them would put
# artifacts in the repository that look like evidence and are not. The
# exception is lifted, and this comment deleted, when the re-run produces
# reports worth citing.
/.poorai/evaluations/

# The campaign directories from those same runs, for the same reason.
#
# Their tool-failure rate was never measured, the context reaching the backend
# was not the one calibrated, and a workspace with no checks scored as
# resolved. thresholds.md declares them void. Committing them would put
# artifacts in the repository that look like evidence and are not; they stay on
# the machine that made them until the corpus is re-run.
/.poorai/evaluations-controls/
/.poorai/evaluations-generation/
/.poorai/evaluations-m6/
/.poorai/evaluations-m6-final/
/.poorai/evaluations-m6-post/
/.poorai/evaluations-maxctx/
/.poorai/evaluations-realistic/

# macOS Finder metadata.
.DS_Store
